msgid "User attributes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/_static/badges/ent-plus.rst:9
msgid ""
"|plans-img-yellow| Available on `Enterprise and Enterprise Advanced plans"
" <https://mattermost.com/pricing/>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../<rst_prolog>:6
msgid "plans-img-yellow"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:7
msgid ""
"From Mattermost v10.8, ensure your teams always have the critical "
"information they need to collaborate effectively by defining and managing"
" organization-specific user profile attributes as system attributes that "
"you can synchronize with your AD/LDAP or SAML identity provider."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:9
msgid ""
"System attributes enable you to customize user profile attributes to "
"match your organization's unique needs and streamline collaboration while"
" keeping user data centralized and consistent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:11
msgid ""
"From Mattermost v11, you have enhanced control over these user attributes"
" through admin-managed vs user-editable settings. By default, attributes "
"are admin-managed for security, but you can explicitly allow user editing"
" for specific attributes that don't impact access control or sensitive "
"organizational data. These user attributes supplement existing user "
"details visible from the user's profile picture."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:13
msgid ""
"Mobile examples of a user profile with user attributes added as system "
"attributes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:17
msgid "Before you begin"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:19
msgid ""
"If you plan to synchronize system properties with your AD/LDAP or SAML "
"identity provider, ensure AD/LDAP or SAML synchronization is already "
"enabled and configured. See the :doc:`AD/LDAP groups </administration-"
"guide/onboard/ad-ldap-groups-synchronization>` product documentation or "
":ref:`SAML 2.0 <administration-guide/configure/authentication-"
"configuration-settings:saml 2.0>` configuration settings documentation "
"for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:23
msgid ""
"From Mattermost v11, user attributes have enhanced admin controls with a "
"security-first approach. All attributes are admin-managed by default, "
"providing better security and governance. System administrators can "
"explicitly enable user editing for specific attributes through the System"
" Console interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:25
msgid ""
"If your organization uses :doc:`attribute-based access control (ABAC) "
"</administration-guide/manage/admin/attribute-based-access-control>`, "
"which requires an Enterprise Edition Advanced license, attributes used in"
" access control policies should remain admin-managed for security "
"reasons. You can enable user-managed attributes for ABAC by setting "
"``EnableUserManagedAttributes`` in ``config.json``, or via an environment"
" variable as noted below, but this should be done with caution:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:27
#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:38
msgid ""
"``config.json`` setting: "
"``\".AccessControlSettings.EnableUserManagedAttributes: false\",`` with "
"options ``true`` and ``false``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:28
#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:39
msgid ""
"Environment variable: "
"``MM_ACCESSCONTROLSETTINGS_ENABLEUSERMANAGEDATTRIBUTES``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:30
msgid ""
"This configuration setting isn't managed using the System Console, and is"
" disabled by default to ensure that access control policies remain secure"
" and can't be circumvented by users modifying their own profile "
"attributes. Learn more about `admin-managed versus user-editable "
"attributes <#admin-managed-vs-user-editable-attributes>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:32
msgid ""
"Additionally, from mobile app v2.31.0, user attributes are fully "
"supported on mobile devices. Mobile users can both view and manage "
"profile attributes (if allowed by admin settings) directly from the "
"mobile app. Mobile attribute support requires the same server-side "
"configuration, and no additional mobile-specific setup is required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:36
msgid ""
"From Mattermost v10.11, user-managed attributes are excluded from ABAC "
"rules for security reasons. If your organization uses ABAC (which "
"requires Enterprise Edition Advanced), a system admin can explicitly "
"enable user-managed attributes for ABAC by setting "
"``EnableUserManagedAttributes`` in ``config.json`` or via an environment "
"variable as noted below. This configuration setting isn't managed using "
"the System Console, and is disabled by default to ensure that access "
"control policies remain secure and can't be circumvented by users "
"modifying their own profile attributes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:41
msgid ""
"Additionally, from mobile app v2.31.0, user attributes are fully "
"supported on mobile devices. Mobile users can both view and manage "
"profile attributes directly from the mobile app. Mobile attribute support"
" requires the same server-side configuration, and no additional mobile-"
"specific setup is required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:45
msgid ""
"From Mattermost Enterprise v10.9, the ability to create and manage system"
" properties as a Mattermost system admin requires no manual setup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:49
msgid ""
"You'll need Mattermost Enterprise v10.8 or later, and be a Mattermost "
"system admin to enable the system properties feature flag, "
"``MM_FEATUREFLAGS_CUSTOMPROFILEATTRIBUTES`` to create and manage system "
"properties. See the Mattermost developer documentation for details on "
"`enabling feature flags in a self-hosted deployment "
"<https://developers.mattermost.com/contribute/more-info/server/feature-"
"flags/#self-hosted-and-local-development>`_. Mattermost Cloud customers "
"can request this feature flag be enabled by contacting their Mattermost "
"Account Manager or by `creating a support ticket "
"<https://support.mattermost.com/hc/en-"
"us/requests/new?ticket_form_id=11184911962004>`_ request."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:52
msgid "Admin-managed vs user-editable attributes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:54
msgid ""
"From Mattermost v11, system administrators have enhanced control over "
"user attributes through admin-managed vs user-editable settings. This "
"distinction provides better security and governance for organizational "
"profile data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:56
msgid "**Admin-managed attributes** (default behavior):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:58
msgid "Controlled exclusively by system administrators"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:59
msgid "Users cannot edit these values in their profiles"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:60
msgid ""
"Recommended for security-sensitive information like roles, clearance "
"levels, or organizational identifiers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:61
msgid ""
"Ideal for attributes used in ABAC (Attribute-Based Access Control) "
"policies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:62
msgid ""
"Values can only be updated by admins or through identity provider "
"synchronization"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:64
msgid "**User-editable attributes**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:66
msgid "Users can update these values in their own profiles"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:67
msgid "System administrators can still modify these attributes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:68
msgid ""
"Appropriate for non-sensitive information like personal preferences, "
"skills, or contact details"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:69
msgid "Should not be used for attributes that impact security access controls"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:72
msgid ""
"For security reasons, attributes used in ABAC policies are admin-managed "
"by default and cannot be edited by users unless explicitly enabled by a "
"system administrator through the **Allow user editing** option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:74
msgid "**Best practices:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:76
msgid ""
"Keep attributes that affect access control or contain sensitive "
"organizational data as admin-managed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:77
msgid ""
"Only enable user editing for attributes that don't impact security "
"policies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:78
msgid ""
"Regularly review user-editable attributes to ensure they remain "
"appropriate for user management"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:79
msgid ""
"Consider your organization's data governance requirements when "
"determining attribute editability"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:82
msgid "Add attributes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:84
msgid ""
"You can define and manage up to 20 system attributes using the System "
"Console. Each attribute becomes a user profile option users can populate,"
" unless you disable the **Editable by Users** option, available from "
"Mattermost v11. Once you reach the maximum of 20 attributes, you can't "
"create new attributes until you `delete attributes <#manage-"
"attributes>`__ you no longer need."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:88
msgid ""
"When you disable the **Editable by Users** option for an attribute, only "
"admins can set its value using :ref:`mmctl cpa <administration-"
"guide/manage/mmctl-command-line-tool:mmctl cpa>` commands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:90
msgid ""
"In the System Console, go to **Site Configuration > System Attributes > "
"User Attributes** and select **Add Attribute**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:91
msgid "Enter the following details:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:93
msgid ""
"**Attribute name**: Enter a unique name for the attribute. Attribute "
"names can be up to 40 characters long."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:94
msgid "**Type**: Specify the type of attribute as one of the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:96
msgid "**Text** for text-based profile attributes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:97
msgid "**Phone** for phone number-based profile attributes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:98
msgid "**URL** for web site address-based profile attributes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:99
msgid ""
"**Select** for a list of profile attribute values users can choose from. "
"Specify each value followed by pressing **TAB** or **ENTER**. Values can "
"be up to 64 characters long, and users can choose a single value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:100
msgid ""
"**Multi-select** for a list of profile attribute values users can select "
"from. Specify each value followed by pressing **TAB** or **ENTER**. "
"Values can be up to 64 characters long, and users can choose multiple "
"values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:102
msgid "Specify the attribute's visibility as one of the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:104
msgid "**Always show**: The attribute is always visible in user profiles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:105
msgid ""
"**Hide when empty**: The attribute is only visible in user profiles when "
"it has a value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:106
msgid "**Always hide**: The attribute is never visible in user profiles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:109
msgid ""
"If an attribute is created or updated without explicit visibility or sort"
" order (for example via API or automation), Mattermost returns default "
"values in responses even if those attributes weren't stored. Visibility "
"defaults to the server's default visibility, and sort order defaults to "
"``0``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:111
msgid ""
"Configure user editing permissions (Mattermost v11 or later) by enabling "
"or disabling the **Editable by users** option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:113
#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:146
msgid "Save your changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:117
msgid ""
"Duplicate existing attributes by selecting **More** |more-icon| and "
"selecting **Duplicate attribute**. This creates a new attribute with the "
"same name and type as the original attribute. You can then edit the new "
"attribute to change its name, type, and visibility as needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../<rst_prolog>:16
msgid "Use the More icon to access additional message options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:120
msgid "Manage attributes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:122
msgid ""
"**Modify**: Select the attribute fields to make inline changes to the "
"attribute's name, type, or values. Select **More** |more-icon| to change "
"a attribute's visibility."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:124
msgid ""
"**Order**: Control the order you want attributes to appear in user "
"profiles by dragging and dropping them in the list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:126
msgid ""
"**Delete**: Delete attributes you no longer need or want by selecting "
"**More** |more-icon| and selecting **Delete property**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:129
msgid ""
"When updating user attributes via API or automation, the ``attrs`` object"
" replaces existing attribute settings rather than merging. If you send "
"only visibility, the sort order resets to ``0`` unless you include "
"``sort_order`` in the same request. If a patch fails, the API may return "
"the error string \"Unable to patch User Attribute field\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:131
msgid ""
"**User Edit Permissions**: From Mattermost v11, all user attributes are "
"admin-managed by default for enhanced security. To allow user editing for"
" specific attributes, administrators can enable this through the **More**"
" |more-icon| menu and selecting **Allow user editing**. This should only "
"be enabled for attributes that do not impact security access controls or "
"organizational policies. Attributes used in ABAC policies should remain "
"admin-managed unless there's a specific business need and the security "
"implications are fully understood."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:133
msgid ""
"**Edit User Attribute Values**: From Mattermost v11.1, you can view and "
"update user attribute values for individual users through the System "
"Console. See the :ref:`Manage user attributes <administration-"
"guide/configure/user-management-configuration-settings:manage user "
"attributes>` documentation for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:135
msgid ""
"In cases where multiple system admins manage system attributes, refresh "
"your web browser instance to see real-time updates to system attributes "
"made by other admins."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:138
msgid "Sync attributes with your identity provider"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:140
msgid ""
"Synchronize a attribute with AD/LDAP or SAML by selecting **More** |more-"
"icon| and selecting **Link attribute to AD/LDAP** or **Link attribute to "
"SAML**. Mattermost takes you directly to the **AD/LDAP** or **SAML 2.0** "
"configuration settings page in the System Console where you can map the "
"attributes you want to synchronize."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:142
msgid ""
"Scroll to the **User attributes sync** section to specify the attribute "
"used to populate the attribute in user profiles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/admin/user-attributes.rst:144
msgid ""
"Specify the attribute mapping for the attribute by entering the attribute"
" name in the system attribute's **Attribute** field. The attribute name "
"must match the attribute name in your identity provider."
msgstr ""

